WEBVTT

1
00:00:07.598 --> 00:00:14.380
In 1996 at the start of the twenty-sixth Olympic Games in Atlanta, Georgia, this great American hero lit

2
00:00:14.400 --> 00:00:15.260
the Olympic flame.

3
00:00:16.220 --> 00:00:17.000
Who is this man?

4
00:00:17.580 --> 00:00:19.181
Why is he a great American hero?

5
00:00:20.081 --> 00:00:21.361
These are difficult questions.

6
00:00:22.142 --> 00:00:25.903
To answer them we must go back over fifty years.

7
00:00:26.003 --> 00:00:30.484
In 1942, when our hero was born, he was given the name Cassius Clay.

8
00:00:31.296 --> 00:00:35.339
He was born into a poor, working-class, black family in Louisville, Kentucky.

9
00:00:36.139 --> 00:00:39.842
When Cassius was a teenager, life for black families was very hard.

10
00:00:40.862 --> 00:00:47.247
While white Americans were becoming rich, building nice houses, and going to good schools, black Americans were still

11
00:00:47.307 --> 00:00:47.907
very poor.

12
00:00:49.548 --> 00:00:53.131
Cassius Clay never liked his name because it was a white man's name.

13
00:00:54.051 --> 00:00:58.494
It was not a name that came from his ancestors, but rather it was the name of the

14
00:00:58.534 --> 00:01:01.136
slave owner who had owned his family years before.

15
00:01:02.332 --> 00:01:07.355
As a child, Cassius Clay was furious with how white Americans treated black Americans.

16
00:01:08.516 --> 00:01:14.019
When Cassius was 12, he started to box under the instructions of a policeman named Joe Martin.

17
00:01:14.859 --> 00:01:18.121
Martin and others immediately saw that Cassius was a great boxer.

18
00:01:18.821 --> 00:01:24.364
By the time he was 17, he had won a very important championship for young boxers: the Golden

19
00:01:24.404 --> 00:01:25.465
Gloves Championship.

20
00:01:28.226 --> 00:01:34.253
Then in 1960, at the age of 18, Cassius went to the Olympics in Rome and won a

21
00:01:34.293 --> 00:01:34.813
gold medal.

22
00:01:35.573 --> 00:01:38.794
He was on his way to becoming one of the greatest boxers in history.

23
00:01:39.754 --> 00:01:44.096
After Cassius won a gold medal at the Olympics, he became a professional boxer.

24
00:01:45.016 --> 00:01:47.677
His goal was to become the Heavyweight Champion of the World.

25
00:01:49.437 --> 00:01:51.738
This is the highest title that a boxer can receive.

26
00:01:52.578 --> 00:01:54.399
Cassius quickly became very famous.

27
00:01:55.059 --> 00:01:58.920
This was because he was not only a great boxer, but a good showman as well.

28
00:01:59.808 --> 00:02:02.329
He would make up sayings about himself and other boxers.

29
00:02:02.810 --> 00:02:07.092
His most famous line was: "I float like a butterfly and sting like a bee."

30
00:02:08.213 --> 00:02:11.174
Cassius always said that he was the greatest boxer ever.

31
00:02:11.875 --> 00:02:16.437
This made some people angry because he was so young and he had not yet fought the greatest

32
00:02:16.497 --> 00:02:17.458
boxers of the time.

33
00:02:18.198 --> 00:02:21.960
But Cassius was a great boxer, and he had a new style of boxing.

34
00:02:23.021 --> 00:02:30.128
On February 25, 1964, he fought Sonny Liston, the greatest boxer at that time, for the title of

35
00:02:30.168 --> 00:02:31.689
Heavyweight Champion of the World.

36
00:02:32.769 --> 00:02:35.450
Of course everyone thought that Liston would easily win.

37
00:02:36.450 --> 00:02:38.150
Cassius was called the underdog.

38
00:02:39.111 --> 00:02:41.171
That means everyone thought he was going to lose.

39
00:02:41.991 --> 00:02:43.112
It was a very good fight.

40
00:02:44.032 --> 00:02:46.013
Both men fought hard for a long time.

41
00:02:48.073 --> 00:02:54.415
Suddenly, to everyone's surprise, Cassius knocked out Liston and won the match, becoming the Heavyweight Champion of the

42
00:02:54.455 --> 00:02:58.476
World! Two days later Cassius joined the Nation of Islam.

43
00:02:59.124 --> 00:03:03.007
This is a group of black people who are committed to Allah and who take care of their

44
00:03:03.047 --> 00:03:06.269
bodies by not smoking, drinking, or acting immorally.

45
00:03:07.930 --> 00:03:10.772
They also fight for a better life for black people in America.

46
00:03:11.473 --> 00:03:16.376
At this time Cassius Clay gave up the slave name that he hated so much and chose a

47
00:03:16.416 --> 00:03:17.817
name based on his new religion.

48
00:03:18.638 --> 00:03:21.040
Since then he has been called Muhammad Ali.

49
00:03:23.741 --> 00:03:27.144
Muhammad Ali reached his goal and became the greatest boxer in the world.

50
00:03:27.944 --> 00:03:32.146
Over the next three years, he fought in many matches and won every one of them.

51
00:03:33.027 --> 00:03:34.648
He was truly the greatest fighter ever.

52
00:03:35.488 --> 00:03:38.050
Then something very terrible happened to Muhammad Ali.

53
00:03:39.951 --> 00:03:46.234
On April 28, 1967, Muhammad Ali was drafted into the United States Army to fight in the war

54
00:03:46.274 --> 00:03:46.934
in Vietnam.

55
00:03:47.655 --> 00:03:52.778
However, he did not want to go to Vietnam because his religion taught him this war was not

56
00:03:52.838 --> 00:03:56.800
just. Ali did not want to kill people who were not his enemies.

57
00:03:58.356 --> 00:04:03.818
Because he refused to join the army, his title of Heavyweight Champion was taken away from him, and

58
00:04:03.838 --> 00:04:06.338
he was not allowed to box anywhere in the United States.

59
00:04:07.259 --> 00:04:13.960
Then on June 20, 1967, a formal trial was held by the government, and Ali was convicted of

60
00:04:14.000 --> 00:04:15.141
refusing to join the army.

61
00:04:15.941 --> 00:04:17.742
He was sentenced to five years in prison.

62
00:04:18.822 --> 00:04:23.023
During the late 1960s, Ali was very active in the Civil Rights Movement.

63
00:04:23.683 --> 00:04:26.404
He encouraged black people to stand up against white people.

64
00:04:26.976 --> 00:04:30.998
Finally in 1970 Ali was allowed to continue his boxing career.

65
00:04:31.538 --> 00:04:36.440
Over the next ten years, Muhammad Ali proved that he truly was the greatest boxer in the world.

66
00:04:39.401 --> 00:04:42.522
As Ali got older, he strengthened his religious beliefs.

67
00:04:43.143 --> 00:04:45.784
He no longer hates white people like he did when he was young.

68
00:04:46.664 --> 00:04:51.926
He believes that all people must work together to create a better world and prepare themselves for heaven.

69
00:04:53.907 --> 00:04:56.648
Because Ali was a great boxer, he earned a lot of money.

70
00:04:57.664 --> 00:04:59.885
However, he has shared his money with the poor.

71
00:05:00.386 --> 00:05:04.688
He gave money to build schools, hospitals, and Islamic religious centers.

72
00:05:05.328 --> 00:05:11.572
In 1981, after 22 years of boxing, Ali retired with one of the best records of all time.

73
00:05:12.352 --> 00:05:15.193
In his career he competed in 61 fights.

74
00:05:15.794 --> 00:05:18.395
He won 56 of them and only lost 5.

75
00:05:19.776 --> 00:05:24.999
A year after he retired, doctors discovered that Ali had an illness called Parkinson's disease.

76
00:05:25.899 --> 00:05:30.598
Because of this disease, Ali is not able to speak well, and he moves very slowly.

77
00:05:31.299 --> 00:05:33.920
However, his disease has not affected his mind.

78
00:05:34.361 --> 00:05:35.802
He still thinks very clearly.

79
00:05:37.102 --> 00:05:43.106
To honor Muhammad Ali for his great contributions to sports and society, he was chosen to light the

80
00:05:43.166 --> 00:05:47.029
Olympic flame at the start of the twenty-sixth Olympic games in Atlanta, Georgia.

81
00:05:47.629 --> 00:05:51.152
And now you know why Muhammad Ali is a great American hero.
